# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend/.gitignore — this file travels with the backend repo on the VPS, so it
# must be self-sufficient. Do NOT rely on the repo root .gitignore.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets. The root .gitignore also covers .env, but once backend/ is pushed as
# its OWN repository the root file is not present, and this would have shipped
# DB_PASS, JWT_SECRET, SMTP_PASS and the Meta access token to GitHub.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Runtime state — MUST stay on disk across deploys, MUST never be in git.
# These hold the logged-in WhatsApp session (a full Chrome profile). Committing
# one leaks a live WhatsApp login, and losing one forces every number to be
# re-paired by hand.
uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep
.wwebjs_cache/

# Patch files ARE tracked (nothing to un-ignore here — deliberately NOT
# ignored). package.json runs `patch-package` on postinstall, and the
# whatsapp-web.js patch is what keeps a paired QR session alive on newer
# WhatsApp Web builds. When patches/ was ignored, postinstall silently no-oped
# on the VPS (it ends in `|| echo "Patch applied or skipped"`) and deployed an
# unpatched whatsapp-web.js that drops sessions right after pairing.
#
# If a patch file ever conflicts with your local node_modules, fix the conflict
# in the patch itself. Do not ignore this directory.

# Logs and crash dumps
*.log
logs/
pm2-logs/

# Local tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build / test artefacts
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local database dumps taken before a migration. The .js migration scripts in
# migrations/ and scripts/ ARE tracked; only ad-hoc dumps are ignored.
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

